    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7357-6129'
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/carpentries-incubator/ML_with_AWS_SageMaker
url: >-
  https://carpentries-incubator.github.io/ML_with_AWS_SageMaker/index.html
abstract: >-
  A Carpentries-style lesson on running machine learning
  workflows on AWS without losing control of the bill. It
  covers SageMaker notebooks as lightweight controllers,
  S3 data setup, training and hyperparameter-tuning jobs
  (XGBoost and PyTorch, CPU vs. GPU, parallel instances),
  retrieval-augmented generation on Amazon Bedrock, on a
  rented GPU notebook, and as Processing jobs (the WattBot
  energy-literature challenge), and fine-tuning an
  open-weight vision-language model with LoRA as a training
  job (the Badger Scribe handwriting-transcription
  challenge, German Kurrent letters from the UW-Madison
  Max Kade Institute). Cost control runs through every
  episode: cost-allocation tags on every resource, runtime
  caps on every job, written cost estimates compared to the
  bill, and explicit cleanup. Designed for researchers and
  practitioners who want scalable, cost-conscious ML
  workflows on cloud infrastructure.
